 "notes": [
  "The RSS commands are the most reliable, structured sources: get-news-feed (/rss/<name>.xml) for news and get-podcast-episodes (/podcasts/rss/<slug>.rss) for podcasts. Use list-rss-feeds to find valid feed names.",
  "The recording did not show the markup of the HTML listing pages (search, tags, sections, authors, schedules, Life, podcasts, video). Their extract selectors are generic link selectors and may also return navigation links. Filter results by URL pattern: /news/<section>/<id>/<slug>, /life/<category>/<slug>, /podcast/<slug>.",
  "Article URLs have the form /news/<section>/<numeric id>/<slug>. Split a URL from a listing to get the arguments for get-news-article.",
  "Radio programme pages such as /national/programmes/mediawatch redirect (301) to /podcast/<slug>. Pass that slug to get-podcast-episodes.",
  "/news redirects (308) and /news/latest redirects (302). Use get-news-feed or list-section-news for the latest stories.",
  "durations in get-video are in milliseconds. The Brightcove policy key in the accept header may be truncated in the recording; if get-video fails with an auth error, the key needs refreshing from the site's player config.",
  "Explored without a login. All commands are public reads."
